//
// Gate E cell: a vector a lambda appends to is shared through the closure's pointer as a read one is (`@FR-L-CapHeap`, no cell); the body's `c += [x]` builds the literal as a value whose `_vec_N` first names the capture, pushes the item onto the capture itself, and appends the value (`OpAppendVector(capture, {Vector …}, 0)`).
// Prints: [1,2,3,4] 4

fn main() {
  c = [1];
  add = fn(x: integer) { c += [x]; };
  add(2);
  c += [3];
  add(4);
  println("{c} {len(c)}");
}
